From: pattex67 <33281022+pattex67@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 18:34:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 25/25] Texture cache: a render target over part of a mip chain
 can rescale (Kirby Air Riders' update at 2x)

The updated game renders its race at a dynamic 1712x960 over its 2048x1152 mip chains.
Those render targets have one level, but an alias that is a chain kept them from
rescaling, so the depth buffer went down and back up again (dot grid, dark characters).
ImageCanRescale now skips aliases that are mip_chain_rescaleable when scaling up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
index 7da064ad81..b460eb7e21 100644
--- a/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/texture_cache/texture_cache.h
@@ -2595,6 +2595,12 @@ bool TextureCache<P>::ImageCanRescale(ImageBase& image) {
     image.flags |= ImageFlagBits::CheckingRescalable;
     for (const auto& alias : image.aliased_images) {
         Image& other_image = slot_images[alias.id];
+        // A render target over part of a mip chain (Kirby Air Riders' updated version renders
+        // its race at a dynamic 1712x960 over its 2048x1152 chains): the chain follows it.
+        if (other_image.info.mip_chain_rescaleable &&
+            !Settings::values.resolution_info.downscale) {
+            continue;
+        }
         if (!ImageCanRescale(other_image)) {
             image.flags &= ~ImageFlagBits::CheckingRescalable;
             return false;
-- 
